    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107234,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107235,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephroma is localized in the kidney.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107236,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephroma may manifest as a palpable abdominal mass or be detected on screening in a child with a germline <em>DICER1</em> mutation and/or pleuropulmonary blastoma. About 25% of cases are bilateral {24481001}. Cystic nephromas are typically treated by complete nephrectomy.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107237,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephroma occurs slightly more often in boys than in girls. Most patients are aged &lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;years (median: 16&nbsp;months). Cases are rare in patients aged &gt;&nbsp;4&nbsp;years {26772403}. Familial cases of cystic nephroma and an association with pleuropulmonary blastoma were recognized in the early 1990s {8382107}. Cystic nephroma is now considered a pathognomonic neoplasm in <em>DICER1</em> syndrome {21266384}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107238,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephroma is associated with <em>DICER1</em> mutations in about 90% of cases {24481001}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107239,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mouse models with conditional ablation of <em>DICER1</em> in ureteric bud epithelium during development show cystic masses of the kidney resembling cystic nephroma {20944551}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107240,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephromas are generally large tumours, with a median diameter of about 100&nbsp;mm and a median weight of 540&nbsp;g. They are usually well circumscribed and consist entirely of cysts of variable size and shape, and they have no macroscopically noticeable expansive, solid nodules. In many cases, there is a direct continuity between the tumour and the pelvicalyceal structures {26772403}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107241,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephromas are sharply demarcated from the renal parenchyma in about 55% of cases, and poorly demarcated in the rest. They are composed entirely of cysts separated by septa of different thicknesses. The septa are lined by flattened, cuboidal, or hobnailing epithelium. The septa are usually thin and hypocellular, and they contain fibrous tissue with focal cellular condensations and well-differentiated tubules, but no blastema&nbsp;&ndash; its presence is a diagnostic criterion for cystic partially differentiated nephroblastoma {26772403}. ER and PR staining may be absent, unlike in adult cystic nephroma {15578885}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107242,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107243,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Germline analysis of tumour-specific <em>DICER1</em> mutations may be helpful in the diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107244,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a circumscribed neoplasm composed of epithelial-lined cysts separated by fibrous septa, which typically contain bland mesenchymal cells and chronic inflammation.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>DICER1</em> mutations may be detected.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107245,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107246,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 256,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephroma is treated with surgery only, usually by complete nephrectomy, or in selected cases by partial nephrectomy {19172100}. Its prognosis is excellent, with event-free and overall survival rates of 100% {17162067}. Very rare cases of cystic nephroma transformation into <em>DICER1</em> sarcoma have been described, but the risk is regarded as very low {24481001}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T10:28:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]